> write a poem about the sea at night, four stanzas, then a short title
The Sea at Night

The sea is a symphony of sound,
A lullaby of waves that pound,
A gentle rhythm, a soothing lull,
A dance of darkness, a nighttime hurl.

The moon above, a silver arc,
A beacon in the starry dark,
A silver path that leads the way,
To where the sea meets the nighttime day.

The stars above, a glittering show,
A dance of light, a celestial flow,
A dance of constellations, a nighttime sight,
A dance of wonder, a starry night.

The sea is a mystery, a secret to keep,
A place of wonder, a place to sleep,
A place of peace, a place to be,
The sea at night, a place to see.

